{% band words=["Listen.","Distil.","Remember.","Move."] note="The one full-bleed inversion in the piece. Its job is to break the reading rhythm exactly once." /%}

The work was not to replace the first idea, but to make it unmistakable.

{% spec columns=1 heading="The G was the start. The Ø made it ours." standfirst="How the mark arrived at itself, in four moves." items=[{"num":"01","key":"Preserve","heading":"Keep the useful grammar","body":"The first idea already held three relevant cues: a letter, a recording target, and a needle. The work was not to replace that thought, but to make it unmistakable."},{"num":"02","key":"Enlarge","heading":"Let the mark fill the object","body":"Early frames spent too much space on cream surround and layered bevels. The chosen form grows until the symbol, rather than the container, owns the Dock."},{"num":"03","key":"Name","heading":"Move from G to Ø","body":"The wildcard became the answer. The slash in GRØD's Ø already carries direction. Turn its centre into a listening aperture and the name becomes the mechanism."},{"num":"04","key":"Print","heading":"Trade clinical polish for memory","body":"Warm paper, dense ink, halftone edges, and slight misregistration make the icon feel handled. The software is precise. The identity is allowed to feel human."}] /%}

{% spec columns=3 heading="Three readings. One motion." standfirst="The symbol works because it never settles into a single explanation." detail="It can be read as the Ø in GRØD, the centre of a recording, or a needle turning attention into forward movement. None of those meanings needs to be illustrated literally. Their overlap is the identity." items=[{"num":"Ø","key":"Name","glyph":"/studies/grod-icon/read-name.svg","ink":"brand","heading":"Ownership","body":"The Scandinavian letter is specific to GRØD and gives the mark ownership."},{"num":"◎","key":"Attention","glyph":"/studies/grod-icon/read-attention.svg","ink":"teal","heading":"Listening","body":"The open centre reads as a listening point rather than a passive badge."},{"num":"↗","key":"Direction","glyph":"/studies/grod-icon/read-direction.svg","ink":"#48234F","inkDark":"#C79BD0","heading":"Consequence","body":"The long diagonal turns capture into consequence: notes, decisions, and what comes next."}] /%}

{% swatches heading="Colour with a job." items=[{"hex":"#D41467","job":"Recording energy"},{"hex":"#168A96","job":"Signal and echo"},{"hex":"#48234F","job":"Direction and depth"},{"hex":"#F3E7CF","job":"Warm paper"}] /%}

{% glyphs heading="Keep the gesture. Lose the print." standfirst="The menu-bar family should inherit the open circle, pivot, and directional diagonal from Listening Ø. It should not inherit paper, colour, halftone, shadow, or frame." grounds={"paper":"Light menu bar","ink":"Dark menu bar"} marks=[{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/mb-idle.svg","label":"Idle"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/mb-detected.svg","label":"Detected"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/mb-recording.svg","label":"Recording"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/mb-paused.svg","label":"Paused"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/mb-processing.svg","label":"Processing"}] note="Directional study only. Final masters require pixel-fitting at 16 pt and 18 pt." /%}

{% spec columns=1 items=[{"num":"01","body":"Preserve the diagonal in every state. It is the bridge back to the primary icon."},{"num":"02","body":"Let state live at the pivot. Recording, pause, and processing should not replace the identity."},{"num":"03","body":"Use black plus alpha as a macOS template. The system supplies light and dark colour."},{"num":"04","body":"Pulse only for a nudge. Active recording, pause, and processing must remain unmistakable."}] /%}

{% scaleProof heading="One gesture, from poster to pixel." rungs=[{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/primary-256.webp","size":256,"label":"256 px","caption":"Dock / Spotlight"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/primary-128.webp","size":128,"label":"128 px","caption":"Dock working size"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/primary-64.webp","size":64,"label":"64 px","caption":"Compact UI"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/primary-32.webp","size":32,"label":"32 px","caption":"Circle and slash still resolve"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/primary-16.webp","size":16,"label":"16 px","caption":"A silhouette test, not a menu-bar asset"},{"src":"/studies/grod-icon/secondary-64.webp","size":64,"label":"Secondary","caption":"Signal Stamp, for when the needle would dominate"}] /%}

{% plate
   src="/studies/grod-icon/secondary-512.webp"
   alt="The GRØD Signal Stamp secondary mark — a teal outer ring, raspberry centre, and aubergine pivot on warm paper."
   eyebrow="Secondary mark"
   heading="Signal Stamp."
   lede="Less instrument. More imprint."
   captionLead="Secondary — Signal Stamp."
   caption="Flatter, quieter, and immediate at reduced size." /%}

The secondary retains the concentric signal logic but removes the physical needle. It is quieter, flatter, and more immediate at reduced size. The primary remains the face of the app.

{% spec columns=1 heading="Where the secondary belongs." standfirst="Two marks, one hierarchy — the secondary supports, it never substitutes." items=[{"key":"Use for","body":"Compact editorial marks, supporting graphics, internal tools, and moments where the long needle would dominate."},{"key":"Do not use","body":"As an interchangeable primary, or as the menu-bar glyph. Hierarchy is the point."}] /%}

{% spec columns=1 heading="Hold the character. Reduce the noise." standfirst="The working contract for carrying Listening Ø into product surfaces without turning the identity into a collection of loosely related targets." items=[{"num":"01","key":"Primary artwork","heading":"One master, one dominant read","body":"1024×1024 RGBA, genuine exterior transparency. Raspberry Ø, aubergine needle, restrained teal misregistration — kept clear of the macOS mask's safe area, with texture that stays visible at large sizes and steps aside for silhouette below 64 px."},{"num":"02","key":"Hierarchy","heading":"Two marks, ranked","body":"Listening Ø is the default identity and the public-facing hero. Signal Stamp is the sole supporting full-colour mark. The menu bar is a purpose-built monochrome descendant, never a reduced app icon — and earlier directions remain process history, not public alternatives."},{"num":"03","key":"Optical sizing","heading":"Judge the silhouette first","body":"Keep full grain and edge character at 128 px and above. From 64 down to 32 px, judge the aperture and diagonal first and quiet everything else. Below 32 px, prefer the secondary or a dedicated monochrome descendant — and at 16 to 18 pt, redraw rather than shrink."},{"num":"04","key":"Material rules","heading":"Keep the handling, not the shine","body":"Keep warm stock, ink density, selective halftone, and minor register drift. Avoid glass rims, chrome, glossy reflections, synthetic glow, or hard plastic. Geometry stays deliberate even when the ink edge is imperfect — the same discipline behind the promise underneath it: your meeting content never leaves this Mac."}] /%}

## Fewer marks. Better memory.

Two marks are enough. Listening Ø leads. Signal Stamp supports it. The remaining explorations have done their job and can move out of the live identity set while staying preserved as design history.

- **Primary** — Listening Ø. Lead.
- **Secondary** — Signal Stamp. Support.
- **Menu bar** — Listening gesture. Redraw.
- **Others** — Exploration archive. Retain, do not promote.
